lf-contract 0.1
# sha-ch is an IR 0.2 word (src/program/sha-words.fs uses LSHIFT and
# -ROT): leanforth verify refuses it, since its receipt needs schema 0.4,
# which awaits the owner's [format] gate (plan 8.4.1k). Contract language
# 0.1 has no bitwise operations either; what the word computes is proved by
# Lean (shaCh_correct in tests/reference/program-ir.lean) and its export
# re-checked by LeanForth (make reference-program-sha-export). This
# contract states only the range of the result. No expect line: the
# outcome is the refusal, not one of the generator's.
id sha-ch/0
word sha-ch
ir tests/program/ir/sha-words.ir
stack ( x y z -- u )
inputs x y z
statement For 32-bit words x, y, z the word returns a 32-bit word (FIPS 180-4's Ch(x, y, z), which this contract language cannot state).
pre 0 <= x && x <= 4294967295
pre 0 <= y && y <= 4294967295
pre 0 <= z && z <= 4294967295
case true
  out r
  ensure 0 <= r && r <= 4294967295
